---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../lib/site";

const title = `About us — ${site.name}`;
const description =
  "Learn about GST on MRP, a free and private GST calculator for India that helps you extract or add GST and see clear CGST, SGST and IGST breakdowns.";
---

<PageLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/about"
  eyebrow="About"
  heading="About GST on MRP"
  intro="A simple, honest tool that makes Indian GST easy to understand for shoppers, students, freelancers and small businesses."
>
  <p>
    <strong>GST on MRP</strong> began with an everyday frustration: you buy
    something at its printed price and have no easy way to see how much of it is
    tax. Because the Maximum Retail Price already includes GST, the tax sits
    hidden inside the number on the label. We built this tool to make that
    hidden portion visible in seconds.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <p>
    We provide two straightforward calculators. The first works in reverse,
    pulling the base price and GST out of an inclusive MRP. The second adds GST
    on top of a pre-tax amount to give you the final price. Both instantly show
    the split into CGST, SGST and IGST, so you always understand where the tax
    goes.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Shoppers who want to know the real value behind a price tag.</li>
    <li>Freelancers and small businesses preparing quick estimates.</li>
    <li>Students and professionals learning how GST works in practice.</li>
    <li>Anyone double-checking a bill or invoice on the go.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Our principles</h2>
  <p>
    We care about three things: speed, clarity and privacy. The calculator runs
    entirely in your browser, so nothing you type is sent to a server or stored
    anywhere. There are no sign-ups, no tracking of your amounts and no limits
    on how often you can use it.
  </p>

  <h2>A note on accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    Our results follow the standard GST formulas and are rounded to two decimal
    places, which is ideal for quick checks and everyday understanding. For
    official filings, invoices or legal purposes, please confirm the figures
    against current government rules and your accounting software, since rounding
    conventions and rate classifications can vary.
  </p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    Have a question, suggestion or correction? We would love to hear from you on
    our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. You can also read our
    <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> and
    <a href="/terms-and-conditions">terms &amp; conditions</a> to learn more
    about how the site works.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
